| `agents.tool_max_output_bytes` | integer | `67108864` | a whole number, 1 or more and at most `sys.maxsize`, the longest a Python bytes object can be | `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`tool_limits`, `run_tool`), for the same five callers as `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` | Sets how many bytes one tool child, or the action server's doer, may write to stdout or to stderr: one byte past it ends the child's session and refuses the call as `ChildOutputTooLarge` naming this key, with the same exits as a timeout. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] agents.tool_max_output_bytes = 67108864` to stderr. | a model reply's size: `models.max_reply_bytes` | always |
